  <section id="posle">
    <h2>After surgery</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Discharge is usually 2–3 days after surgery. Mild swelling and numbness of the skin around the wound are common and gradually go away.</li>
      <li>Medication continues for life: surgery removes the plaque, not atherosclerosis itself.</li>
      <li>Follow-up ultrasound — after a few months, then on the schedule set by your doctor.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="srochno" slot="urgent">
    <h2>When to seek urgent help</h2>
    <div class="callout alert">
      <p>Sudden weakness or numbness of an arm, leg or half of the face, speech problems, loss of vision in one eye — even if it quickly passed — <strong>call emergency services immediately (112; 103 in Russia).</strong> After neck surgery — also with rapidly increasing neck swelling, difficulty breathing or swallowing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
